205
00:10:59,995 --> 00:11:06,541
[SPEAKER_00]: That all those thoughts that I'm... are because of the agitation... are recognized because of the agitation.

206
00:11:06,561 --> 00:11:07,802
[SPEAKER_00]: The agitation comes first.

207
00:11:08,663 --> 00:11:10,245
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, therefore, there's nothing I can do

208
00:11:11,325 --> 00:11:16,469
[SPEAKER_00]: To get rid of that agitation, because everything I can do is get... is part of... within this mood.

209
00:11:16,489 --> 00:11:26,016
[SPEAKER_00]: So... so... it's the same... that's the same sort of structure as the body, in that it's like a container for a long...

210
00:11:26,597 --> 00:11:32,141
[SPEAKER_00]: But you're asking what's the relationship between those two, between the conscious body and the mood.

211
00:11:32,281 --> 00:11:36,344
[SPEAKER_01]: You describe the relation between the mood and the thoughts, which would have been my next question.

212
00:11:36,645 --> 00:11:36,985
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

213
00:11:37,963 --> 00:11:39,884
[SPEAKER_01]: As in consciousness, mind, thoughts.

214
00:11:40,065 --> 00:11:42,106
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

215
00:11:42,806 --> 00:11:44,207
[SPEAKER_01]: It's... it's the same principle.

216
00:11:44,488 --> 00:11:44,968
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

217
00:11:44,988 --> 00:11:46,169
[SPEAKER_00]: Of all these... all...

218
00:11:46,729 --> 00:11:48,050
[SPEAKER_00]: Thoughts are always within a mood.

219
00:11:48,350 --> 00:11:49,391
[SPEAKER_00]: Mood is always within a body.

220
00:11:50,652 --> 00:11:51,032
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

221
00:11:51,633 --> 00:11:51,813
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

222
00:11:52,613 --> 00:11:55,055
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not that the mood comes first, but that's the thing.

223
00:11:55,155 --> 00:12:03,481
[SPEAKER_01]: Practically, for a mind that's not freed from ignorance, what comes first is the thoughts.

224
00:12:03,501 --> 00:12:03,761
[SPEAKER_00]: Thoughts.

225
00:12:03,781 --> 00:12:04,221
[SPEAKER_00]: Thoughts.

226
00:12:04,241 --> 00:12:04,822
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

227
00:12:05,409 --> 00:12:07,191
[SPEAKER_01]: Within thoughts, you get to discern the mood.

228
00:12:08,292 --> 00:12:19,224
[SPEAKER_01]: Obviously, if you don't abandon the lack of understanding in regard to the nature of the right order, you would then still think the thoughts come first and then...

229
00:12:20,215 --> 00:12:23,317
[SPEAKER_01]: Blame them for your moods and for everything else.

230
00:12:23,957 --> 00:12:25,038
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to go against the stream.

231
00:12:25,058 --> 00:12:26,038
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

232
00:12:26,078 --> 00:12:29,660
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your thoughts come first, practically speaking, because that's where ignorance has taken you.

233
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,421
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your starting point.

234
00:12:31,981 --> 00:12:33,282
[SPEAKER_01]: But within that, you discern the mood.

235
00:12:33,622 --> 00:12:36,084
[SPEAKER_01]: Initially, you discern the mood secondary to the thoughts.

236
00:12:36,104 --> 00:12:36,964
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you blame the thoughts.

237
00:12:36,984 --> 00:12:38,145
[SPEAKER_01]: You try to stop thinking thoughts.

238
00:12:38,165 --> 00:12:40,426
[SPEAKER_01]: So, a lot of meditation techniques, they will prevent you from thinking.

239
00:12:41,006 --> 00:12:42,067
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't get into a bad mood.

240
00:12:42,687 --> 00:12:51,955
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, if you were pointed rightly, you get to understand that thoughts and simultaneously present mood, it's actually the mood comes first, structurally, so to speak.

241
00:12:51,975 --> 00:12:53,076
[SPEAKER_01]: They're there at the same time.

242
00:12:53,685 --> 00:12:55,146
[SPEAKER_01]: But the mood is more general.

243
00:12:55,286 --> 00:12:56,966
[SPEAKER_01]: The mood is more fundamental.

244
00:12:57,226 --> 00:13:02,689
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically, there's nothing I can do in regard to these thoughts that will get below that mood.

245
00:13:02,729 --> 00:13:04,269
[SPEAKER_00]: That mood... Or step outside of it.

246
00:13:04,349 --> 00:13:05,009
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly, yeah.

247
00:13:05,109 --> 00:13:05,270
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

248
00:13:05,530 --> 00:13:06,870
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever you do, it's going to be rooted in that mood.

249
00:13:06,890 --> 00:13:10,352
[SPEAKER_00]: Any manipulation I do on those thoughts is all within that mood.

250
00:13:10,592 --> 00:13:10,712
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

251
00:13:10,752 --> 00:13:11,752
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't step outside of it.

252
00:13:11,772 --> 00:13:14,833
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what we've been talking about so extensively.

253
00:13:14,893 --> 00:13:17,634
[SPEAKER_01]: Like the things you can attend to, things you can think about.

254
00:13:17,674 --> 00:13:17,894
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

255
00:13:18,215 --> 00:13:19,735
[SPEAKER_01]: And then the peripheral in regard to it.

256
00:13:19,775 --> 00:13:21,736
[SPEAKER_01]: First, you discern peripheral as secondary to it.

257
00:13:22,103 --> 00:13:24,985
[SPEAKER_01]: But then you realize, no, peripheral is the container, the primary container.

258
00:13:25,025 --> 00:13:25,365
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

259
00:13:26,086 --> 00:13:28,207
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's how you get to get the sign of the mind.

260
00:13:28,227 --> 00:13:28,347
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

261
00:13:28,367 --> 00:13:29,388
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what I was just going to say.

262
00:13:29,408 --> 00:13:29,968
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the mind.

263
00:13:30,129 --> 00:13:36,093
[SPEAKER_00]: You discern the sign of the mind in regard to your thoughts, in regard to, like, actual present experience that you attend to.

264
00:13:36,593 --> 00:13:43,998
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why it's such a wrong view to think you can attend to your mind in the same sense you attend to other objects, including thoughts, because thoughts are mental objects.

265
00:13:44,058 --> 00:13:44,258
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

266
00:13:44,839 --> 00:13:45,779
[SPEAKER_01]: Objects of the mental sense.

267
00:13:45,799 --> 00:13:46,560
[SPEAKER_01]: That I can attend to.

268
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:49,202
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, the sights are objects of the visual sense

269
00:13:50,355 --> 00:13:51,956
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there's thought... many thoughts going on.

270
00:13:51,996 --> 00:13:52,997
[SPEAKER_00]: Some thoughts are peripheral.

271
00:13:53,217 --> 00:13:54,318
[SPEAKER_00]: There are peripheral thoughts.

272
00:13:54,338 --> 00:13:54,538
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

273
00:13:54,818 --> 00:14:05,806
[SPEAKER_00]: But... but the mind is something... is that thing that's the sort of background of those thoughts that I cannot attend to.

274
00:14:07,327 --> 00:14:07,948
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's the thing.

275
00:14:07,968 --> 00:14:15,633
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you... as I said, you start... you have to start first with thoughts, then discern the mind rightly, in the right order.

276
00:14:15,753 --> 00:14:17,254
[SPEAKER_01]: The mind is that which is the first.

277
00:14:17,354 --> 00:14:18,135
[SPEAKER_01]: Thoughts are secondary.

278
00:14:18,499 --> 00:14:21,581
[SPEAKER_01]: So, any movement of my thought in regard to my mood is within the mood.

279
00:14:21,822 --> 00:14:22,042
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

280
00:14:22,762 --> 00:14:27,766
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's discernment of the mood that will free you from the mood, not the particular set of movements of your thoughts.

281
00:14:27,886 --> 00:14:29,367
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

282
00:14:29,647 --> 00:14:32,710
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you can go further, following the same principle.

283
00:14:32,890 --> 00:14:43,438
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you get established in that notion of your own mind, that peripheral sign, that peripheral container of what the mood is, you also then get to see what's peripheral to that.

284
00:14:44,172 --> 00:14:49,854
[SPEAKER_01]: So, can I just... What is a necessary basis for having any mood in the other day, regardless of the thoughts that might be moving within it?

285
00:14:50,254 --> 00:14:51,355
[SPEAKER_00]: Conscious body, having a body.

286
00:14:51,655 --> 00:14:52,255
[SPEAKER_01]: Being alive.

287
00:14:52,275 --> 00:14:52,515
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

288
00:14:52,895 --> 00:14:55,016
[SPEAKER_01]: Having a beating heart or operating body.

289
00:14:55,756 --> 00:14:58,477
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize that is the peripheral container to your mood.

290
00:14:58,557 --> 00:14:58,777
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

291
00:15:00,498 --> 00:15:01,218
[SPEAKER_00]: That comes first.

292
00:15:01,378 --> 00:15:01,538
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

293
00:15:02,459 --> 00:15:03,519
[SPEAKER_01]: Then you can't get underneath that.

294
00:15:03,539 --> 00:15:03,899
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

295
00:15:03,919 --> 00:15:08,041
[SPEAKER_01]: And that doesn't disappear when you go down to these lower levels of thoughts or whatever.

296
00:15:08,061 --> 00:15:08,801
[SPEAKER_01]: It just stays there.

297
00:15:09,301 --> 00:15:09,421
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

298
00:15:09,441 --> 00:15:11,582
[SPEAKER_01]: The only thing what happens to it, it gets ignored.

299
00:15:12,938 --> 00:15:15,680
[SPEAKER_01]: The right order gets ignored and that's why you jump into assuming the wrong order.

300
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:18,682
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's possible for it not to be, because it is always there.

301
00:15:18,702 --> 00:15:20,964
[SPEAKER_00]: It's implicit in the mood, it's implicit in the thoughts.

302
00:15:21,004 --> 00:15:21,965
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, it's always there, yeah.

303
00:15:22,045 --> 00:15:22,865
[SPEAKER_00]: It's always there.

304
00:15:22,925 --> 00:15:24,286
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the closest thing to you.

305
00:15:24,467 --> 00:15:27,189
[SPEAKER_00]: If you understood that it can't not be there, then you wouldn't forget that it was there.

306
00:15:27,209 --> 00:15:32,753
[SPEAKER_01]: It's impossible to forget it is there, because forgetfulness is within that thing having to be there.

307
00:15:32,833 --> 00:15:33,033
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

308
00:15:33,633 --> 00:15:35,074
[SPEAKER_01]: It's determined by being alive.

309
00:15:35,094 --> 00:15:35,875
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you can forget.

310
00:15:38,287 --> 00:15:39,328
[SPEAKER_00]: Can I say something?

311
00:15:39,848 --> 00:15:42,409
[SPEAKER_00]: I used to think...

312
00:15:43,249 --> 00:15:48,791
[SPEAKER_00]: I found it helpful to think of the mind as being like the light in the room.

313
00:15:50,352 --> 00:15:55,514
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I'm looking at you now and I can't see the light.

314
00:15:57,254 --> 00:15:58,595
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it certainly resembles the nature.

315
00:15:58,615 --> 00:16:00,676
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not something I can see and yet I know there's light.

316
00:16:00,696 --> 00:16:01,976
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't attend to the light.

317
00:16:01,996 --> 00:16:04,297
[SPEAKER_00]: You can only think things that were revealed by the light.

318
00:16:04,848 --> 00:16:05,028
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

319
00:16:05,048 --> 00:16:05,949
[SPEAKER_00]: But I know that there's light.

320
00:16:06,009 --> 00:16:06,509
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not that...

321
00:16:06,529 --> 00:16:08,450
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't have any doubt about whether there's light in the room.

322
00:16:08,470 --> 00:16:09,250
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course, of course, yeah.

323
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,071
[SPEAKER_00]: And you have to think about it either.

324
00:16:11,091 --> 00:16:12,252
[SPEAKER_00]: And I'd have to think about it, yeah.

325
00:16:12,892 --> 00:16:16,133
[SPEAKER_01]: No, that's... yeah, that's the... that implication that I said.

326
00:16:16,453 --> 00:16:21,796
[SPEAKER_01]: The mind is implicit in the thoughts, in as much as the conscious body is implicit within the mind, within the thoughts.

327
00:16:22,016 --> 00:16:22,276
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

328
00:16:24,617 --> 00:16:31,381
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, can you even conceive looking, even perceiving the light, if you have no eyes and no body?

329
00:16:31,621 --> 00:16:31,841
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

330
00:16:32,121 --> 00:16:33,361
[SPEAKER_01]: And no... and you're not alive.

331
00:16:33,441 --> 00:16:33,682
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

332
00:16:34,022 --> 00:16:34,502
[SPEAKER_01]: Impossible.

333
00:16:38,345 --> 00:16:42,788
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that kind of leads to, then, to the final point.

334
00:16:43,908 --> 00:16:45,709
[SPEAKER_01]: So, through your thoughts, you discern your mood.

335
00:16:46,570 --> 00:16:47,891
[SPEAKER_01]: You stop regarding the second.

336
00:16:47,931 --> 00:16:52,834
[SPEAKER_01]: You see there's more primordial, simultaneously enduring, the fundamental container of those thoughts.

337
00:16:53,274 --> 00:16:58,857
[SPEAKER_01]: Within that, you discern further necessary basis for your thoughts, for your mind, which is the conscious body.

338
00:16:58,998 --> 00:17:00,058
[SPEAKER_01]: Body with consciousness.

339
00:17:00,458 --> 00:17:00,839
[SPEAKER_01]: Out there.

340
00:17:01,419 --> 00:17:02,220
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing to do with you.

341
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:03,440
[SPEAKER_01]: He has arose.

342
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:04,641
[SPEAKER_01]: He was born, given.

343
00:17:05,784 --> 00:17:08,406
[SPEAKER_01]: You're fully within it, fully subjected to its nature.

344
00:17:10,887 --> 00:17:11,568
[SPEAKER_00]: Isn't that a thought?

345
00:17:14,790 --> 00:17:19,893
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, but it's a thought that's made possible.

346
00:17:19,913 --> 00:17:20,333
[SPEAKER_00]: By what?

347
00:17:21,494 --> 00:17:22,335
[SPEAKER_00]: By the conscious body.

348
00:17:23,535 --> 00:17:25,917
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, but, see, the conscious body is a thought.

349
00:17:26,137 --> 00:17:26,537
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, so...

350
00:17:27,678 --> 00:17:30,700
[SPEAKER_01]: So, can you experience the conscious body

351
00:17:31,474 --> 00:17:34,155
[SPEAKER_01]: In any other manner than having a thought of it.

352
00:17:34,635 --> 00:17:38,657
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you experience anything without that thing being also a thought there?

353
00:17:39,217 --> 00:17:39,418
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

354
00:17:40,698 --> 00:17:47,021
[SPEAKER_01]: Being, without that thing being fundamentally, primarily, a dhamma, a container, a thing, a thought, yeah, a thing.

355
00:17:47,481 --> 00:17:47,961
[SPEAKER_01]: Impossible.

356
00:17:49,122 --> 00:17:50,422
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what's the difference then?

357
00:17:51,243 --> 00:18:00,947
[SPEAKER_01]: From the starting point of Bhuttujana's thoughts, and then the point after you understand the relationship between the nature of the mind, the nature of the conscious body, and then you realize, well,

358
00:18:01,647 --> 00:18:02,387
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the same thought.

359
00:18:03,368 --> 00:18:04,068
[SPEAKER_01]: What has changed?

360
00:18:04,088 --> 00:18:15,213
[SPEAKER_00]: I guess, seeing the difference between the thought and... And the thought, and the thought.

361
00:18:15,373 --> 00:18:16,054
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, okay.

362
00:18:16,774 --> 00:18:21,196
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, see, those thoughts, those thoughts resist you.

363
00:18:21,256 --> 00:18:21,496
[SPEAKER_01]: Mm-hmm.

364
00:18:22,777 --> 00:18:29,940
[SPEAKER_00]: They're, you know, you find them there, you're subjected to those thoughts.

365
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:30,280
[SPEAKER_01]: Mm-hmm.

366
00:18:32,055 --> 00:18:35,717
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they're sort of... that's their externality, sort of thing.

367
00:18:35,897 --> 00:18:41,041
[SPEAKER_00]: They... there's something beyond me.

368
00:18:44,503 --> 00:18:45,984
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's another thought.

369
00:18:46,344 --> 00:18:48,765
[SPEAKER_00]: That is another thought, but when... like...

370
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:53,048
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a notion of beyond me.

371
00:18:53,788 --> 00:18:54,569
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it's another thought.

372
00:18:54,649 --> 00:18:55,069
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

373
00:18:55,229 --> 00:18:56,410
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's... it's not really beyond.

374
00:18:57,696 --> 00:18:58,817
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you...

375
00:18:58,938 --> 00:19:01,361
[SPEAKER_01]: So, let's, let's, like, again, restart.

376
00:19:01,521 --> 00:19:01,821
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

377
00:19:01,861 --> 00:19:06,668
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have a... you have thoughts of agitation, whatever.

378
00:19:06,968 --> 00:19:08,210
[SPEAKER_01]: You want to get rid of the agitation.

379
00:19:08,770 --> 00:19:11,334
[SPEAKER_01]: Then you recognize the unpleasant mood of that agitation.

380
00:19:11,434 --> 00:19:11,694
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

381
00:19:12,335 --> 00:19:13,677
[SPEAKER_01]: And you stop, eh...

382
00:19:15,455 --> 00:19:17,136
[SPEAKER_01]: Disordering it, so to speak.

383
00:19:17,576 --> 00:19:29,420
[SPEAKER_01]: You stop regarding the mood as a product of your thoughts, but you see that movements of your thoughts are within the container of the mood, which is why they move, which is why they shuffle and try to get... shake off the mood.

384
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:37,503
[SPEAKER_01]: That already frees you from the pressure of the thoughts, by discerning the right order of those thoughts.

385
00:19:39,103 --> 00:19:41,124
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the thought of the mood is a thought.

386
00:19:41,858 --> 00:19:45,220
[SPEAKER_01]: The thought of the agitation within the mood that you want to get rid of is another thought.

387
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:45,661
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

388
00:19:46,301 --> 00:19:50,184
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the difference is just wanting to get rid of it or not.

389
00:19:50,204 --> 00:19:52,185
[SPEAKER_01]: Wanting to get rid... And why do you want to get rid of it?

390
00:19:52,946 --> 00:19:56,628
[SPEAKER_01]: What is the necessary condition for wanting to get... What is the necessary condition for craving?

391
00:19:58,169 --> 00:19:58,910
[SPEAKER_00]: Painful feeling.

392
00:20:00,170 --> 00:20:00,491
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

393
00:20:00,911 --> 00:20:03,152
[SPEAKER_01]: But something in regard to the painful feeling.

394
00:20:03,813 --> 00:20:04,814
[SPEAKER_01]: What's the necessary condition?

395
00:20:05,414 --> 00:20:08,336
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, you know, you can remove the craving and still have painful feeling.

396
00:20:10,306 --> 00:20:12,868
[SPEAKER_01]: But what is it that you cannot have, if you remove the craving?

397
00:20:15,569 --> 00:20:17,150
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, the assumption of the wrong order.

398
00:20:17,811 --> 00:20:18,251
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, I see.

399
00:20:18,291 --> 00:20:18,591
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

400
00:20:19,212 --> 00:20:25,176
[SPEAKER_01]: You will not be trying to get rid of it, unless you assume that you can get rid of it by getting rid of it.

401
00:20:26,156 --> 00:20:31,300
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the movements you engage in are rooted in the assumption that you can... that moving can get rid of it.

402
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:36,523
[SPEAKER_00]: By understanding the order, by seeing the order in the right way, that's right.

403
00:20:36,543 --> 00:20:37,364
[SPEAKER_00]: Your whole mood changes.

404
00:20:37,384 --> 00:20:39,225
[SPEAKER_00]: Your mood, your whole kind of...

405
00:20:39,590 --> 00:20:41,191
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you're out of the mood, you're beyond it.

406
00:20:41,211 --> 00:20:41,391
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

407
00:20:41,692 --> 00:20:44,274
[SPEAKER_00]: Because... You're truly beyond it, because you're not affected by it anymore.

408
00:20:44,374 --> 00:20:45,895
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no need...

409
00:20:45,955 --> 00:20:46,816
[SPEAKER_01]: It's completely pointless.

410
00:20:46,936 --> 00:20:50,959
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why, like, if you say, theoretically, yes, it's just thoughts.

411
00:20:51,119 --> 00:20:51,339
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

412
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:53,301
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything is just thoughts.

413
00:20:53,321 --> 00:20:53,441
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

414
00:20:53,801 --> 00:20:56,904
[SPEAKER_01]: In a sense that, yeah, determined by the physical conscious body.

415
00:20:57,104 --> 00:20:57,364
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

416
00:20:58,064 --> 00:21:01,767
[SPEAKER_01]: But, within the thoughts, there is the right order of the thoughts.

417
00:21:01,988 --> 00:21:02,228
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

418
00:21:02,748 --> 00:21:04,690
[SPEAKER_01]: There is the right nature and there is the wrong order.

419
00:21:04,830 --> 00:21:07,672
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the sole difference between a Bhutujana and an Arahant.

420
00:21:08,325 --> 00:21:17,312
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I mean, like, oh, you go, you get to understand your mood on account of the thoughts, then you get to understand the necessary basis for both mood and the thoughts that move within the mood, is this conscious body.

421
00:21:18,132 --> 00:21:25,157
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you abandon that for understanding the nature of it, which is, yeah, you were subjected to, you were given, you have no say, it's on the level of the elements, pretty much.

422
00:21:25,898 --> 00:21:29,621
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you realize, oh, so I'm back onto the thoughts, as I always was.

423
00:21:29,841 --> 00:21:31,342
[SPEAKER_01]: I couldn't have left it even if I wanted to.

424
00:21:31,362 --> 00:21:32,703
[SPEAKER_01]: You couldn't have been outside of your thought.

425
00:21:33,374 --> 00:21:37,736
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why, for an arahant, in what's thought, there is only things that have been thought.

426
00:21:38,216 --> 00:21:39,597
[SPEAKER_01]: In the scene, there's just a scene.

427
00:21:39,917 --> 00:21:41,217
[SPEAKER_01]: In the thought, there is just a thought.

428
00:21:41,817 --> 00:21:43,058
[SPEAKER_01]: In the herd, there's just a herd.

429
00:21:44,158 --> 00:21:46,539
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it can't be anything else.

430
00:21:46,599 --> 00:21:53,042
[SPEAKER_01]: But, see, in the scene, there is just a scene, means, in the scene, there is no more wrong order of the scene.

431
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:56,641
[SPEAKER_01]: In the thought, there is no more wrong order of the thought.

432
00:21:56,761 --> 00:21:59,062
[SPEAKER_01]: So, literally, in the scene, there is just scene.

433
00:21:59,102 --> 00:22:00,202
[SPEAKER_01]: There is nothing else there.

434
00:22:00,682 --> 00:22:03,443
[SPEAKER_01]: For Puttujāna, there is the whole world of difference there.

435
00:22:03,803 --> 00:22:08,265
[SPEAKER_01]: The world that's not outside of the scene, or result of the scene.

436
00:22:08,365 --> 00:22:13,487
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just the world that's the result of the wrong order of the scene, or the thought, or any other sense.

437
00:22:13,767 --> 00:22:17,688
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically, getting the order right changes the significance of things.

438
00:22:19,097 --> 00:22:28,942
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, getting the order right, basically, what it means, prevents the gratuitous maintenance of the sense of ownership, the sense of self, the sense of conceit.

439
00:22:29,402 --> 00:22:34,285
[SPEAKER_00]: But what I mean is, like, everyone can say, oh, I know what a thought is.

440
00:22:34,765 --> 00:22:34,905
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

441
00:22:35,893 --> 00:22:39,875
[SPEAKER_00]: But, if you get the right order, then, when you say thought... Well, there are certain...

442
00:22:40,115 --> 00:22:42,897
[SPEAKER_01]: When you say thought, you're talking about what the Buddha meant when he said thoughts.

443
00:22:42,917 --> 00:22:44,058
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

444
00:22:44,078 --> 00:22:45,138
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's a... that's a different thing.

445
00:22:45,218 --> 00:22:45,979
[SPEAKER_01]: No, that's... that's what I mean.

446
00:22:45,999 --> 00:22:49,901
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's when people say, like, they would read the sutta, and then, oh, yeah, okay.

447
00:22:50,121 --> 00:22:50,341
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

448
00:22:50,441 --> 00:22:50,981
[SPEAKER_01]: I understand it.

449
00:22:51,021 --> 00:22:51,221
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

450
00:22:52,002 --> 00:22:57,285
[SPEAKER_01]: So, sure, you understand it on some level, but then you have to see, understanding this, what does that result in?

451
00:22:57,805 --> 00:23:01,847
[SPEAKER_01]: What are the symptoms of having understand... having... having this understood?

452
00:23:03,281 --> 00:23:15,588
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, symptom is you're unable to... means you're unable to suffer, means you have destroyed birth, aging, death, sickness, anything that you're subjected to cannot possibly disturb any, like, completely effortless indifference.

453
00:23:16,388 --> 00:23:18,430
[SPEAKER_01]: Equanimity is not something you must latch on to.

454
00:23:18,970 --> 00:23:20,611
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the result of your understanding.

455
00:23:21,151 --> 00:23:25,033
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're utterly unshakable as a result of your understanding.

456
00:23:25,714 --> 00:23:27,274
[SPEAKER_01]: So, do you still think you understood the thought?

457
00:23:27,675 --> 00:23:29,516
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

458
00:23:29,636 --> 00:23:30,917
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's always the main problem.

459
00:23:30,977 --> 00:23:31,657
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not really like

460
00:23:32,662 --> 00:23:33,883
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't have the right thoughts".

461
00:23:33,943 --> 00:23:37,665
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like thinking that you have understood that which you haven't.

462
00:23:37,945 --> 00:23:38,165
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

463
00:23:38,385 --> 00:23:40,786
[SPEAKER_01]: To that degree, you won't make effort to understand it.

464
00:23:40,826 --> 00:23:41,287
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

465
00:23:42,567 --> 00:23:43,088
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's what I mean.

466
00:23:43,108 --> 00:23:48,531
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, you read the sutta, it makes sense, and you think you understood consciousness, you think you understood the mind, you think you understood the thought.

467
00:23:48,651 --> 00:23:48,851
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

468
00:23:49,471 --> 00:23:51,332
[SPEAKER_01]: Just... you just need to tidy it up a bit more.

469
00:23:53,173 --> 00:24:02,078
[SPEAKER_01]: If you understood any of those, for what it is, if you understood what thought within a thought is, in thought there is just a thought, you would be an arahant.

470
00:24:02,198 --> 00:24:02,398
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

471
00:24:03,258 --> 00:24:05,259
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, on the other hand, well, no, I'm not.

472
00:24:06,279 --> 00:24:09,420
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, I can't take for granted my understanding of this.

473
00:24:09,580 --> 00:24:10,721
[SPEAKER_00]: I have an understanding of it.

474
00:24:11,401 --> 00:24:12,381
[SPEAKER_00]: Which gives me direction.

475
00:24:12,481 --> 00:24:15,803
[SPEAKER_00]: And I could, well, because it makes sense to me, I can think that's right.

476
00:24:16,123 --> 00:24:18,264
[SPEAKER_00]: But, actually, it makes sense to me, but it's not right.

477
00:24:18,284 --> 00:24:24,166
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's what I mean, like, you, like, a person interested in practice should be very careful about

478
00:24:25,195 --> 00:24:36,017
[SPEAKER_01]: Falling into this theoretical statement, so to speak, that then they deem are true and applicable to them as well.

479
00:24:36,097 --> 00:24:38,418
[SPEAKER_01]: The Buddha said in the scene, there is just the scene.

480
00:24:38,518 --> 00:24:40,858
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, so in the scene, there is just the scene.

481
00:24:42,579 --> 00:24:44,379
[SPEAKER_01]: That's only true for an arahant.

482
00:24:46,560 --> 00:24:47,620
[SPEAKER_01]: So if you're not an arahant,

483
00:24:48,041 --> 00:24:50,802
[SPEAKER_01]: For you, there is much more in the scene than just the scene.

484
00:24:50,922 --> 00:25:02,548
[SPEAKER_01]: And yes, if you make the effort and get rid of the more, undo the more, understand the more, which is understand the wrong order and thus rectify it, then yes, in the scene, there has always been just the scene.

485
00:25:02,728 --> 00:25:03,269
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's true.

486
00:25:04,429 --> 00:25:05,770
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's not true to say it when you...

487
00:25:05,990 --> 00:25:09,212
[SPEAKER_01]: It's literally saying like, oh, I have...

488
00:25:09,232 --> 00:25:10,672
[SPEAKER_01]: I have, I don't know, some...

489
00:25:11,933 --> 00:25:13,234
[SPEAKER_01]: I have a flu, whatever.

490
00:25:13,774 --> 00:25:14,214
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm sick.

491
00:25:15,235 --> 00:25:15,415
[SPEAKER_01]: And...

492
00:25:17,673 --> 00:25:19,554
[SPEAKER_01]: The cure for this sickness is such and such.

493
00:25:20,935 --> 00:25:21,436
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's it.

494
00:25:22,877 --> 00:25:23,898
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm still sick.

495
00:25:23,958 --> 00:25:30,182
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, are you free from your sickness on account of knowing that cure?

496
00:25:30,402 --> 00:25:30,523
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

497
00:25:30,543 --> 00:25:31,523
[SPEAKER_01]: It means it's not a cure.

498
00:25:31,924 --> 00:25:34,125
[SPEAKER_01]: It means you don't know enough of it or something.

499
00:25:34,826 --> 00:25:41,991
[SPEAKER_01]: Either way, the point is to be free from sickness, not to have a theoretical knowledge of the cure that then you kind of infer.

500
00:25:42,491 --> 00:25:44,593
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, this applies to me because it applies to everyone.

501
00:25:44,613 --> 00:25:45,694
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a universal truth.

502
00:25:46,154 --> 00:25:46,935
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, but you're still sick.

503
00:25:47,984 --> 00:25:50,806
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it is a universal truth that in the seen there's just the seen.

504
00:25:50,866 --> 00:25:51,686
[SPEAKER_01]: There can't be anything else.

505
00:25:52,987 --> 00:25:58,391
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why when people jump, like, you know, when the Buddha talks about the element of nibbāna, it's there, present.

506
00:25:59,211 --> 00:26:04,194
[SPEAKER_01]: And then people develop the view, oh, so we are already in nibbāna.

507
00:26:05,155 --> 00:26:05,315
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

508
00:26:05,335 --> 00:26:08,757
[SPEAKER_01]: Because element of nibbāna, as in nibbāna, is always present in every one experience.

509
00:26:08,777 --> 00:26:10,358
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter if you're enlightened or not.

510
00:26:10,838 --> 00:26:13,060
[SPEAKER_01]: It means we are already all in nibbāna.

511
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:13,800
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing to be done.

512
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:14,461
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

513
00:26:14,741 --> 00:26:16,642
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it means we are all already healthy.

514
00:26:17,515 --> 00:26:21,737
[SPEAKER_01]: And you say that while you're still very much sick, and subjected to sickness.

515
00:26:22,518 --> 00:26:26,500
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I said, theoretically, it's true, but it's completely wrong for you, because you are still sick.

516
00:26:28,060 --> 00:26:33,303
[SPEAKER_01]: And you will remain in the element of nibbāna, but you will not develop the nibbāna, because you... for as long as you remain sick.

517
00:26:35,444 --> 00:26:36,705
[SPEAKER_01]: Because then you realize, so, what is nibbāna?

518
00:26:36,725 --> 00:26:42,148
[SPEAKER_01]: The knowing that nibbāna is the element, as in possibility, for everyone of us.

519
00:26:42,986 --> 00:26:49,992
[SPEAKER_01]: Is that the same to say as, oh, no, you've made the effort and attained a nibbāna as a result of it, free from suffering, free from conceivings?

520
00:26:50,813 --> 00:26:53,015
[SPEAKER_01]: No, it's the whole world of difference there.

521
00:26:54,055 --> 00:26:59,300
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, element possibility of nibbāna is there, but it doesn't mean that you have fully developed the actual nibbāna.

522
00:27:01,101 --> 00:27:11,130
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's you intentionally trying to obscure the difference between possible nibbāna, which is present, and the actual nibbāna, which is the possible nibbāna that has been developed.

523
00:27:11,917 --> 00:27:15,258
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means you're free from symptoms on account of not having developed a nibbāna.

524
00:27:15,798 --> 00:27:18,899
[SPEAKER_00]: But, yes, nibbāna is part of everyone's experience.

525
00:27:19,499 --> 00:27:21,319
[SPEAKER_01]: The possibility of it.

526
00:27:21,659 --> 00:27:23,380
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what we refer to the element of it.

527
00:27:23,400 --> 00:27:27,540
[SPEAKER_00]: It means, yes, if you do things rightly, you can actualize that possibility.

528
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:31,501
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, it's not like... it's not like something you create, but it's something you discern.

529
00:27:31,601 --> 00:27:32,001
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

530
00:27:32,161 --> 00:27:32,582
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

531
00:27:32,602 --> 00:27:32,822
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

532
00:27:32,862 --> 00:27:33,982
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's... that's not...

533
00:27:34,002 --> 00:27:37,003
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm just pointing out that... Well, like, you know, those suttas.

534
00:27:37,283 --> 00:27:38,283
[SPEAKER_01]: I spoke about it recently.

535
00:27:39,278 --> 00:27:41,838
[SPEAKER_01]: I've done the whole essay on it, the luminous mind.

536
00:27:42,759 --> 00:27:47,019
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, the mind is radiant, luminous, not inhibited by anything.

537
00:27:48,340 --> 00:27:52,460
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's these gratuitous defilements that inhibit it.

538
00:27:52,520 --> 00:27:55,461
[SPEAKER_01]: So, defilements cannot really inhibit the luminosity of the mind.

539
00:27:56,501 --> 00:27:59,401
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's true for an arahant and for somebody who is free from the defilements.

540
00:27:59,461 --> 00:28:08,223
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, in hindsight, you can know, as I said, in hindsight, when you arrive, that, oh, so this is a thought, but now the thought that has uprooted the whole wrong order, and then you realize,

541
00:28:08,930 --> 00:28:09,850
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, it's still a thought.

542
00:28:09,930 --> 00:28:11,951
[SPEAKER_01]: It could have not been anything else from the start.

543
00:28:12,211 --> 00:28:12,451
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

544
00:28:13,211 --> 00:28:15,451
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can only say that once you abandon the wrong order.

545
00:28:15,751 --> 00:28:22,272
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can only say that the mind was truly always luminous and radiant and uninhibited once you have abandoned the defilement of it.

546
00:28:23,053 --> 00:28:27,713
[SPEAKER_01]: And the only reason you can abandon the defilement of it is because they can't truly defile the mind.

547
00:28:29,954 --> 00:28:36,375
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's hard for people to recognize, well, theoretically this is true, but practically my situation starts from the opposite end.

548
00:28:37,277 --> 00:28:40,279
[SPEAKER_01]: So, for Putujana, he has to... he starts with defilements.

549
00:28:40,799 --> 00:28:43,701
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not true for him to say that mind is pure.

550
00:28:44,942 --> 00:28:48,324
[SPEAKER_01]: Otherwise, he'll fall into a view that my mind is pure regardless of my sickness.

551
00:28:49,545 --> 00:29:01,212
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why the Buddha, when, depending on the context and who he was talking to, he would say, like, if he talks to Putujana about the five aggregates or about the mind, he would then say, for an arahant, five aggregates have ceased.

552
00:29:01,913 --> 00:29:02,913
[SPEAKER_01]: Consciousness is gone.

553
00:29:04,114 --> 00:29:05,175
[SPEAKER_01]: All the aggregates are gone.

554
00:29:06,066 --> 00:29:12,389
[SPEAKER_01]: So, oh, because, yes, Putujana's aggregates, which are the aggregates of the wrong order, the only aggregates he can know of, are completely gone.

555
00:29:12,409 --> 00:29:13,550
[SPEAKER_01]: They do not exist as such.

556
00:29:17,632 --> 00:29:18,873
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why you would...

557
00:29:19,553 --> 00:29:31,859
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not always productive to address things on this theoretical level, because then, as I said, somebody who is not free from illness would understand these things in theory and then think, okay, so that's what the understanding of that is.

558
00:29:31,879 --> 00:29:34,841
[SPEAKER_01]: No, if you truly understood it, you would be free from the illness.

559
00:29:34,921 --> 00:29:35,141
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

560
00:29:36,486 --> 00:29:39,987
[SPEAKER_01]: And again, so how does then the mind get polluted, if mind cannot be polluted?

561
00:29:40,467 --> 00:29:41,768
[SPEAKER_01]: That is beginningless.

562
00:29:42,708 --> 00:29:49,850
[SPEAKER_01]: That mistake of thinking the pollution, thinking the mind is like this, when it can't be like that, is beginningless, as the Buddha said.

563
00:29:49,950 --> 00:29:55,912
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no first point, before which avijja wasn't, and then avijja becomes the manifest, that you can discern it.

564
00:29:56,823 --> 00:30:00,024
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, Puthujjana and his view was always as such.

565
00:30:00,724 --> 00:30:04,285
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why once you undo it and you recognize the mind could have not...

566
00:30:04,965 --> 00:30:08,366
[SPEAKER_01]: It made no difference to the mind or the aggregates, your craving and your upādāna.

567
00:30:08,386 --> 00:30:08,526
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

568
00:30:08,586 --> 00:30:09,646
[SPEAKER_01]: Could not have made a difference.

569
00:30:10,286 --> 00:30:12,167
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you understand that, it's irreversible.

570
00:30:12,347 --> 00:30:12,567
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

571
00:30:12,607 --> 00:30:14,567
[SPEAKER_01]: The order was always like that.

572
00:30:14,647 --> 00:30:15,488
[SPEAKER_01]: The order was always right.

573
00:30:15,508 --> 00:30:16,688
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter how you take it.

574
00:30:16,748 --> 00:30:16,968
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

575
00:30:17,108 --> 00:30:19,889
[SPEAKER_01]: But for you, starting point was the assumption of your wrong order.

576
00:30:20,169 --> 00:30:25,110
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why upādāna is responsible for maintenance of the being, of the reality that you know.

577
00:30:25,470 --> 00:30:25,650
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

578
00:30:27,598 --> 00:30:43,888
[SPEAKER_00]: And, and why, like, sort of knowledge of these phenomena that the Buddha is talking about, is really just sort of allowing them to reveal... Yeah, so you remove the assumption of the reality that you know, you realize reality has stayed.

579
00:30:44,068 --> 00:30:45,009
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that was always there.

580
00:30:45,029 --> 00:30:46,530
[SPEAKER_01]: Thoughts have always been the thoughts.

581
00:30:46,570 --> 00:30:48,651
[SPEAKER_01]: In the scene, they have always been just a scene.

582
00:30:49,689 --> 00:30:52,210
[SPEAKER_01]: But it was the whole world of assumption that I had on top of it.

583
00:30:52,710 --> 00:30:53,491
[SPEAKER_01]: And again, that's what I mean.

584
00:30:53,591 --> 00:30:55,452
[SPEAKER_01]: It's irreversible, once you undo it.

585
00:30:55,872 --> 00:31:02,975
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you remove the gratuitous, as the Buddha said, literally, that agantukha was the word, part of it, means like superimposed.

586
00:31:03,555 --> 00:31:03,795
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

587
00:31:04,176 --> 00:31:05,856
[SPEAKER_00]: Means it cannot really become part of it.

588
00:31:05,876 --> 00:31:06,657
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just there.

589
00:31:06,837 --> 00:31:07,617
[SPEAKER_00]: Adventitious.

590
00:31:07,777 --> 00:31:08,517
[SPEAKER_01]: Adventitious.

591
00:31:08,538 --> 00:31:09,558
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

592
00:31:10,238 --> 00:31:18,022
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you remove those gratuitous defilements, the gratuitous there could not have been there, should not have been there, not knowing that you were placing them there.

593
00:31:18,142 --> 00:31:18,342
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

594
00:31:18,900 --> 00:31:21,001
[SPEAKER_01]: You remove it, they cannot come back.

595
00:31:21,101 --> 00:31:21,301
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

596
00:31:21,401 --> 00:31:24,161
[SPEAKER_01]: They cannot return, because there is no room for them.

597
00:31:24,962 --> 00:31:28,723
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what the Buddha meant by upādāna is not in the aggregates.

598
00:31:28,863 --> 00:31:29,883
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not part of the aggregates.

599
00:31:29,903 --> 00:31:31,063
[SPEAKER_01]: It cannot be part of the aggregates.

600
00:31:31,083 --> 00:31:33,464
[SPEAKER_01]: It means five aggregates don't even know about your upādāna.

601
00:31:33,484 --> 00:31:33,744
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

602
00:31:34,244 --> 00:31:34,845
[SPEAKER_01]: You keep putting it there.

603
00:31:34,865 --> 00:31:36,485
[SPEAKER_01]: They're completely unaware of your upādāna, yeah.

604
00:31:36,987 --> 00:31:38,968
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you can't put it there, that's the thing.

605
00:31:38,988 --> 00:31:39,829
[SPEAKER_00]: No, but, well...

606
00:31:39,849 --> 00:31:44,691
[SPEAKER_00]: It says, desire and lust means upādāna is there in regard to the five aggregates.

607
00:31:44,711 --> 00:31:47,213
[SPEAKER_00]: But because you put it... what I mean is, because you put it there, it's there.

608
00:31:47,533 --> 00:31:49,014
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure, that's your starting point.

609
00:31:49,034 --> 00:31:51,835
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the only thing you know, is that this is there.

610
00:31:52,455 --> 00:32:04,862
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have to acknowledge it first, that that's a starting point, and not start practice from this theoretical aspect of aggregates are already free, we are already in nibbāna, mind is already pure, I just need to scratch through the conventional reality until I discover

611
00:32:07,262 --> 00:32:09,504
[SPEAKER_01]: Ultimate is only in response to conventional.

612
00:32:11,105 --> 00:32:13,627
[SPEAKER_01]: So, ultimate is determined by the conventional.

613
00:32:13,747 --> 00:32:15,409
[SPEAKER_01]: Conventional is determined by the ultimate.

614
00:32:16,069 --> 00:32:19,792
[SPEAKER_01]: Either way, you remain ignorant of the nature of reality of any kind.

615
00:32:19,832 --> 00:32:21,614
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter if it's ultimate or conventional.

616
00:32:21,654 --> 00:32:22,455
[SPEAKER_01]: Reality is there.

617
00:32:24,051 --> 00:32:27,692
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the difference is not in reality and the characteristics of reality.

618
00:32:28,053 --> 00:32:30,614
[SPEAKER_01]: The difference is in the wrong order you assume in regard to it.

619
00:32:30,734 --> 00:32:31,114
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

620
00:32:31,754 --> 00:32:34,615
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's not in the conventional reality, nor the ultimate reality.

621
00:32:35,055 --> 00:32:38,257
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, that completely gratuitous division is wrong, utterly wrong.

622
00:32:39,877 --> 00:32:41,858
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the way I would say, even for the targeter.

623
00:32:42,437 --> 00:32:47,779
[SPEAKER_01]: As far as the language goes, as far as the conventions and designations go, the Taoist has understood it.

624
00:32:48,399 --> 00:32:54,122
[SPEAKER_01]: He hasn't blamed it for his ignorance and then replaced it with the greater ultimate reality by removing the veil of maya or something.

625
00:32:54,882 --> 00:32:55,002
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

626
00:32:55,562 --> 00:32:55,922
[SPEAKER_00]: It stays.

627
00:32:56,002 --> 00:32:57,563
[SPEAKER_00]: He still uses words, he still designates.

628
00:32:57,623 --> 00:32:59,984
[SPEAKER_01]: What has changed is the wrong assumption, the wrong order.

629
00:33:00,524 --> 00:33:01,765
[SPEAKER_01]: What comes first, basically.

630
00:33:02,165 --> 00:33:02,565
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

631
00:33:04,266 --> 00:33:09,648
[SPEAKER_01]: And the reason why it's so hard to see is because in thought, there is only a thought.

632
00:33:10,255 --> 00:33:12,717
[SPEAKER_01]: But which one of those thought-thought you put first?

633
00:33:13,017 --> 00:33:13,938
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, exactly.

634
00:33:14,678 --> 00:33:17,600
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, well, whichever it is, it must be wrong, because you're not an arahant.

635
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:17,880
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

636
00:33:18,421 --> 00:33:19,662
[SPEAKER_01]: So, try and do the opposite.

637
00:33:20,062 --> 00:33:20,302
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

638
00:33:20,542 --> 00:33:21,363
[SPEAKER_00]: Go against the stream.

639
00:33:21,383 --> 00:33:22,324
[SPEAKER_00]: Go against the stream.

640
00:33:22,364 --> 00:33:22,924
[SPEAKER_00]: Against the grain.

641
00:33:23,084 --> 00:33:23,284
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

642
00:33:23,985 --> 00:33:27,047
[SPEAKER_00]: Against the grain, yeah.

643
00:33:27,067 --> 00:33:31,150
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's like, oh, consciousness is this, mind is this, thoughts are that.

644
00:33:31,450 --> 00:33:32,311
[SPEAKER_01]: They're all thoughts for you.

645
00:33:32,671 --> 00:33:34,452
[SPEAKER_00]: How can you know consciousness if it's not a thought?

646
00:33:35,693 --> 00:33:35,873
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

647
00:33:36,354 --> 00:33:39,196
[SPEAKER_01]: How can you know your mind, your mood, unless you're thinking it?

648
00:33:40,022 --> 00:33:41,803
[SPEAKER_01]: How can you know your thoughts unless they're being thought?

649
00:33:42,443 --> 00:33:43,744
[SPEAKER_01]: What is the order of those things?

650
00:33:45,925 --> 00:33:51,507
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can only arrive at these things in... with understanding, is if you arrive at them through the right order.

651
00:33:51,987 --> 00:34:01,932
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, in the previous talk, or one of the previous talks we've done, was the... you can only know I, sights and consciousness...

652
00:34:01,952 --> 00:34:02,712
[SPEAKER_00]: Through the contact.

653
00:34:02,732 --> 00:34:03,313
[SPEAKER_01]: Through the pressure.

654
00:34:03,333 --> 00:34:03,933
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

655
00:34:05,290 --> 00:34:07,452
[SPEAKER_01]: So, pressure doesn't disappear when you think about consciousness.

656
00:34:08,013 --> 00:34:11,476
[SPEAKER_01]: Eyes don't disappear... pressure doesn't disappear when you think about the eyes or objects.

657
00:34:12,417 --> 00:34:15,520
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your pressure is where the knowledge is of these things.

658
00:34:16,961 --> 00:34:20,585
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's just emphasizing different aspects within the whole.

659
00:34:21,746 --> 00:34:22,466
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this is the same.

660
00:34:22,507 --> 00:34:24,949
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't, like, oh, now I'm thinking about consciousness.

661
00:34:25,773 --> 00:34:26,753
[SPEAKER_01]: No, you're thinking about your thoughts.

662
00:34:27,773 --> 00:34:29,254
[SPEAKER_01]: And you're thinking about your thoughts within a mood.

663
00:34:30,054 --> 00:34:32,114
[SPEAKER_01]: And you're thinking about the thoughts within a mood about consciousness.

664
00:34:32,735 --> 00:34:35,115
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's always... you're always thinking the same things, which is thoughts.

665
00:34:36,615 --> 00:34:43,497
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just ceasing to assume the, you know, the external point of view, or any form of wrong order, any manifestation of the wrong order.

666
00:34:44,477 --> 00:34:49,878
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what comes first is the thought within a thought of mood, within a thought of the consciousness.

667
00:34:49,898 --> 00:34:52,719
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you think, oh, this is just a thought of consciousness, and then there is consciousness

668
00:34:53,597 --> 00:34:58,939
[SPEAKER_01]: That's another thought that you gave a gratuitous property of being external, real, as opposed to this unreal.

669
00:34:59,039 --> 00:34:59,900
[SPEAKER_00]: Yet, that's another thought.

670
00:34:59,940 --> 00:35:03,521
[SPEAKER_00]: That notion of externality as opposed to internality is another thought.

671
00:35:03,561 --> 00:35:04,141
[SPEAKER_00]: Is another thought.

672
00:35:05,262 --> 00:35:05,642
[SPEAKER_00]: Trapped.

673
00:35:07,003 --> 00:35:07,283
[SPEAKER_01]: Trapped.

674
00:35:07,423 --> 00:35:11,945
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you think that your escape from it is removing the thought, you'll remain trapped forever.

675
00:35:12,205 --> 00:35:12,465
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

676
00:35:13,065 --> 00:35:14,926
[SPEAKER_01]: It's basically just stop assuming the wrong order.

677
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:16,286
[SPEAKER_01]: That is your freedom.

678
00:35:16,947 --> 00:35:20,088
[SPEAKER_00]: That will remove the symptoms of any illness and disease.

679
00:35:20,849 --> 00:35:30,077
[SPEAKER_00]: Which, in another way of saying that, is that whatever can be thought, whatever can be experienced, is impermanent, depends on something that I have no control over.

680
00:35:30,558 --> 00:35:30,738
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

681
00:35:31,439 --> 00:35:33,901
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you experience anything without the conscious body being there?

682
00:35:33,921 --> 00:35:34,081
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

683
00:35:37,884 --> 00:35:40,046
[SPEAKER_01]: And you have not seen it.

684
00:35:40,086 --> 00:35:41,688
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you get to pick and choose your consciousness?

685
00:35:41,808 --> 00:35:41,968
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

686
00:35:42,518 --> 00:35:43,919
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you have to pick and choose your body?

687
00:35:43,939 --> 00:35:44,459
[SPEAKER_01]: Absolutely not.

688
00:35:44,759 --> 00:35:48,101
[SPEAKER_01]: Any difference that you can make to the body is within the body that's given to you.

689
00:35:48,181 --> 00:35:48,341
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

690
00:35:48,601 --> 00:35:49,902
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's only a secondary difference.

691
00:35:50,062 --> 00:35:52,423
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not really a difference of the fundamental nature.

692
00:35:53,363 --> 00:35:54,444
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only borrow the body.

693
00:35:54,904 --> 00:35:55,004
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

694
00:35:55,024 --> 00:35:55,725
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I'm saying.

695
00:35:55,885 --> 00:35:55,985
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

696
00:35:56,005 --> 00:35:57,566
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can use it while it's borrowed, sure.

697
00:35:57,726 --> 00:35:57,966
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

698
00:35:58,246 --> 00:36:00,407
[SPEAKER_00]: But at no point it becomes yours.

699
00:36:00,427 --> 00:36:04,109
[SPEAKER_00]: The only reason you can borrow it is because it's always there.

700
00:36:05,289 --> 00:36:10,352
[SPEAKER_01]: So, not forgetting that context, for example, that whatever you do, whatever you think, whatever you feel, whatever you...

701
00:36:10,885 --> 00:36:12,766
[SPEAKER_01]: You've done whatever you're planning to do.

702
00:36:12,986 --> 00:36:13,827
[SPEAKER_00]: Possibly doing, if you can.

703
00:36:13,887 --> 00:36:18,570
[SPEAKER_01]: It's within the container of the body being there, given to you, conscious body being there, given to you, and you're not saying it.

704
00:36:18,650 --> 00:36:18,891
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

705
00:36:20,832 --> 00:36:24,815
[SPEAKER_01]: And learn how to allow that image, so to speak, to endure peripherally.

706
00:36:25,175 --> 00:36:25,375
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

707
00:36:25,455 --> 00:36:28,297
[SPEAKER_01]: Without you trying to overly attend it and get out of it.

708
00:36:28,517 --> 00:36:29,878
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you can't get out of it.

709
00:36:30,038 --> 00:36:31,860
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only...

710
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:32,260
[SPEAKER_00]: Forget it.

711
00:36:33,941 --> 00:36:37,844
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only basically drain away your sense of self within it.

712
00:36:38,957 --> 00:36:39,377
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

713
00:36:39,818 --> 00:36:44,801
[SPEAKER_01]: By removing any notion of the external ownership, you will remove the basis for maintenance of the sense of self.

714
00:36:45,022 --> 00:36:45,362
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

715
00:36:47,924 --> 00:36:49,185
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, see, it doesn't matter.

716
00:36:49,585 --> 00:36:50,246
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I feel like this.

717
00:36:50,286 --> 00:36:50,946
[SPEAKER_01]: I feel like that.

718
00:36:51,807 --> 00:36:52,507
[SPEAKER_01]: I feel superior.

719
00:36:52,928 --> 00:36:53,728
[SPEAKER_01]: I feel inferior.

720
00:36:53,748 --> 00:36:54,449
[SPEAKER_01]: I feel equal.

721
00:36:55,489 --> 00:36:58,752
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that is possible only because there is this still conscious body there and I'm not saying it.

722
00:36:59,332 --> 00:37:03,415
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, my own sense of self, I undermine by realizing that I cannot own it.

723
00:37:04,016 --> 00:37:05,317
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, it ceases to be myself.

724
00:37:10,774 --> 00:37:16,802
[SPEAKER_01]: So, discerning the context and maintaining the discernment of that context, not attending to the context, because you'll be doing that with yourself.

725
00:37:17,603 --> 00:37:18,484
[SPEAKER_00]: That's not a context.

726
00:37:18,664 --> 00:37:19,004
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

727
00:37:19,905 --> 00:37:21,768
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you start attending it, it ceases to be the context.

